# Definition of Done Checklist

## 📋 **Definition of Done Checklist**

Every task must meet these requirements before completion:

### **Code Quality & Testing**
✅ **Composer test (Pest)** - All tests passing with green status  
✅ **Code coverage** - Minimum 80% coverage on changed lines  
✅ **PHPStan analysis** - Passes at repository's configured level  
✅ **Laravel Pint** - Code style standards met  

### **Frontend & Build**
✅ **npm run lint** - No linting errors or warnings  
✅ **npm run build** - Production build completes successfully  
✅ **Accessibility testing** - WCAG 2.2 AA compliance verified  
✅ **Cross-browser testing** - Functionality verified in target browsers  

### **Security & Validation**
✅ **Input validation** - All user inputs properly validated and sanitized  
✅ **Authorization checks** - Proper permission verification implemented  
✅ **No raw HTML output** - All output properly escaped  
✅ **Security headers** - Appropriate security headers configured  
✅ **CSRF protection** - Cross-site request forgery protection enabled  

### **Documentation & Communication**
✅ **CHANGELOG updated** - Reference this project version  
✅ **API documentation** - New endpoints documented with examples  
✅ **Inline comments** - Complex logic explained clearly  
✅ **Setup instructions** - Environment configuration documented  

### **Pull Request Requirements**
✅ **Clear PR description** including:
- Context and business requirements
- Technical approach and implementation details
- Risk assessment and mitigation strategies
- Rollout plan and rollback procedures
- Testing notes and coverage verification
- Accessibility acceptance criteria
- Performance impact assessment

## 🎯 **Quality Gates**
- **Security Review**: All security requirements met
- **Accessibility Review**: WCAG 2.2 AA compliance verified
- **Performance Review**: No performance regressions introduced
- **Code Review**: Peer review completed and approved
- **Testing Review**: All tests passing with adequate coverage

## ⚠️ **Blocking Criteria**
- Any failing tests
- Security vulnerabilities identified
- Accessibility issues found
- Performance regressions detected
- Code style violations
- Missing documentation
- Incomplete error handling

## 🚀 **Deployment Readiness**
- All quality gates passed
- Staging environment testing completed
- Rollback procedures documented
- Monitoring and alerting configured
- Team notification completed
- Documentation updated